170
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:58,340
That brings us to the one public hearing we're going to do tonight, which was originally scheduled for 640.

171
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:07,700
This is a continued public hearing for an application for a change in use amended site plan review submitted by DJV Properties, LLC.

172
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:15,600
Property is located at Tax Map 10Watt 38-1, also known as 327 Main Street.

173
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:26,820
This application is seeking approval to allow for the construction of a 2,745-square-foot freestanding commercial building, driveway, and parking lot,

174
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:34,180
and to reconfigure the previously approved access for the existing single-family dwelling with attached ADU.

175
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:36,560
Good evening.

176
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:37,680
Good evening.

177
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,140
Good evening.

178
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:50,900
I'm Tom Schaumburg of SEC Associates here on behalf of DJV Properties, LLC.

179
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:58,460
Since the review letter, we have revised the application.

180
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:05,360
Our July 16th response letter addresses each comment as a brief overview.

181
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:12,660
The application now includes high-intensity soil survey mapping, test-fit information, and supporting calculations.

182
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:20,380
Lot coverage calculations demonstrating compliance with Article 2, Part E, Section 5, and architectural floor plans.

183
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:29,680
With building elevations and exterior finish information, a detailed landscape plan has been added as Sheet 5,

184
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:33,400
and an erosion and sedimentation control plan as Sheet 6.

185
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:41,160
The plans now identify all building entrances, pedestrian walkways, ADA-compliant accessible parking and access routes,

186
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:44,660
site lighting, signage, and all proposed utilities.

187
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:58,460
On sewage disposal, soil mapping and calculations conclude availability of 1,458 gallons per day of on-site capacity.

188
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:02,860
The proposed use generates 1,330 gallons per day.

189
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:11,000
It will be 750 for the five existing bedrooms of the existing three-bedroom with two-bedroom attached ADU.

190
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:19,760
480 gallons per day for the 24-seat restaurant with 60 for its three employees, 30 for the dry goods use,

191
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:23,340
and then 10 for its employee, leaving 128 gallons per day remaining.

192
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:31,120
On stormwater, there was a comment about concentrated flow being introduced to the Main Street.

193
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:34,020
Can you talk a little louder, please, just a little bit?

194
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:34,400
Yep.

195
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:39,820
There was a comment about concentrated flow being introduced to Main Street,

196
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,840
so I did take another look at the drainage,

197
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:48,900
and it should be noted that the volume of water in all storm events to the intersection is reduced.

198
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:55,060
Most notably would be in the two-year and the 10-year events where no or very little water is discharged,

199
00:16:55,780 --> 00:17:00,800
as those would be the events that you think you'd generally be worried about in terms of icing in the road.

200
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:03,760
Fairly comfortable with the design.

201
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:09,260
And as far as state permits, again, we are aware that NH DOT driveway permits,

202
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:15,920
water supply, and construction approval for the proposed sewage disposal system are required.

203
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:20,280
We'd like, hopefully, to have these as a condition of approval.

204
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:24,600
We have reviewed the Town Engineer's July 17th letter.

205
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:29,040
Each remaining item is a final plan revision, or item we feel would be appropriate as a condition.

206
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:33,500
With that, we'd respectfully request conditional approval of the application,

207
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:36,300
but I'd be happy to answer any questions the board may have.

208
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,500
Excellent. Thank you.

209
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:41,480
Steve, I see we have a letter from you in here, too?

210
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:42,440
You do.

211
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:52,980
So, as Mr. Schomburg summarized, he responded a lot of his narrative,

212
00:17:53,260 --> 00:18:01,920
and there's a copy of a letter in your packet dated July 16th that SEC prepared

213
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:09,740
in response to my prior report of June 15th.

214
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:15,900
And that, all the companies, the set of drawings,

215
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:19,700
the reduced-size set of drawings that are in your packet tonight.

216
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:32,280
So, after receipt of the cover letter of July 16th and the corresponding set of drawings,

217
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:37,980
I issued, reviewed again, and issued this letter on the 17th the following day.

218
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:43,060
And this is what remains outstanding, is the various state permits.

219
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:47,020
