00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:29,120
Yep.

271
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:33,140
I know there was some confusion with it or some other details.

272
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:33,800
Yeah.

273
00:22:33,980 --> 00:22:47,560
And so, as far as the siting of the driveway for the residents, it's basically located where on the property we can get the required 400 feet of site distance along Main Street that DOT will require.

274
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:51,100
So, we're kind of limited on where we can put the driveway.

275
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:59,080
We know it's not the best location with the intersection, but with it serving just residential traffic for the dwelling.

276
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:09,840
The sight lines, at least, south down Main Street, as well as north on Main Street, as well as Depot Road, are fairly open.

277
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:20,960
And just to put your minds at ease, I mean, I drive in and out of that driveway three or four times a day, rush hour, dump days.

278
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:27,720
And I would have the same concern looking at it from, you know, we've got a bunch of roads coming in the same spot.

279
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:33,240
But when you're actually there and you're sitting there waiting for traffic, you just wait.

280
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:41,140
You know, everybody's got stop signs where you can see all the way down 121A north, see quite a ways down 121A south.

281
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:46,920
It's really a safe, you know, I feel very safe entering the road.

282
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:53,180
So, I can see why you want to make sure that, you know, that didn't create any safety problems.

283
00:23:53,460 --> 00:23:58,120
But, you just, you know, if you try it, you'll see what I'm talking about.

284
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:01,520
You can see every which way and really not bad at all.

285
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:04,500
It's not a high accident spot or anything, right?

286
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:05,240
What's that?

287
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:07,140
Little accidents coming in and out of there.

288
00:24:07,820 --> 00:24:16,900
No, I mean, it's more, you know, if you come in from the dump, you feel like, you know, you have to, it's, you feel like you're, you're really going to look out for traffic.

289
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:18,160
Coming from the north.

290
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:18,680
Yeah.

291
00:24:18,940 --> 00:24:22,220
So, that's a, you know, that's more dangerous than entering from the driveway.

292
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:24,720
You know, the driveway you can see everywhere.

293
00:24:25,340 --> 00:24:25,580
Gotcha.

294
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:26,140
So.

295
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,100
I'm sorry, Steve, were you going to say something?

296
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:36,160
Yeah, I mean, because I, I think the genesis of that conversation was my last report, right?

297
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:36,600
Yep.

298
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:42,340
I guess I accomplished what I sought to do.

299
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:46,700
And that was get Tom to take a good look at it as an engineer.

300
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:47,840
And he asked.

301
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:48,580
Okay.

302
00:24:48,580 --> 00:24:59,260
But it, regardless of the response, the reality is his driveway permitting on the main street is exclusively DR2.

303
00:24:59,520 --> 00:24:59,800
Right.

304
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:00,360
Yeah.

305
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:07,440
But there was a second part of it, too, that's also disappeared because he's taken care of.

306
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:22,460
I was concerned that stormwater from the site would sheet through or down that driveway and end up at that sea of pavement that we have at the intersection of Maine,

307
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:29,940
Fremont and Depo, and that's kind of funky in there.

308
00:25:29,940 --> 00:25:38,500
And I know in the winter, because there's not a lot of grade in there, over the years, highway has had a hard time keeping that free of ice.

309
00:25:38,500 --> 00:25:38,980
Yeah.

310
00:25:38,980 --> 00:25:55,400
So, as Tom indicated in his presentation, he's actually reducing the amount of water that is flowing in that direction that's less than flowing today.

311
00:25:55,400 --> 00:26:02,540
So, I guess he's, so, I mean, you notice that that comment just disappeared from my letter?

312
00:26:02,860 --> 00:26:03,060
Yeah.

313
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:08,440
Because, you know, they went out, they looked at it, they measured the site distance.

314
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,440
They're going to have to for DOT anyways.

315
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:14,860
And they've reached the conclusions that he shared with you tonight.

316
00:26:15,060 --> 00:26:20,040
So, you know, again, I'm glad you did all that.

317
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:21,340
Okay.

318
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:25,980
Any other board members have any questions for the applicant?

319
00:26:27,860 --> 00:26:28,340
Yeah.

320
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:32,040
How many seats, how many people are you going to, how many seats in that restaurant?

321
00:26:32,820 --> 00:26:33,960
It's 24 seats.

322
00:26:34,220 --> 00:26:34,560
24?

323
00:26:35,620 --> 00:26:35,800
Okay.

324
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:48,320
No, the only thing I, I was already here the other night, if there was any way you could get more parking in there, that would be great, but I don't know if you can, but it's pretty hectic in there sometimes.

325
00:26:49,460 --> 00:26:56,860
I mean, the way I look at it is that we're spreading out the traffic by moving bruschettis down the hill and adding parking down there.

326
00:26:57,620 --> 00:27:05,780
We're also going to pick up some spots in the lower parking lot, because we're going to move the dumpsters off that parking lot, which will free up some more space down there.

327
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:08,740
So, it's tight.

328
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:14,380
I mean, it gets busy on, you know, during the weekend mornings, and you're going to have to manage it.

329
00:27:15,140 --> 00:27:30,080
But I feel like we're going to pick up, we are picking up space in front of the new building, and we're just moving one, you know, we're moving bruschettis down there, so we're actually picking up some parking spaces for the two most busy businesses up there.

330
00:27:31,180 --> 00:27:32,460
If that makes sense to you, Ernie.

331
00:27:33,380 --> 00:27:34,540
I guess, kind of.

332
00:27:34,540 --> 00:27:35,540
It sounds like you thought about it.

333
00:27:35,740 --> 00:27:36,420
Yeah, definitely.

334
00:27:36,420 --> 00:27:45,420
I think, too, is the peaks, I think, for each business should kind of fall at different times of the day as well, which should help with kind of spreading it out.

335
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:47,560
Excellent.

336
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:53,340
David, do you know what's going into current bruschettis, and what are you going to do with that space?

337
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:56,400
There's a couple scenarios that I'm working on.

338
00:27:56,520 --> 00:28:05,720
One is that I'm going to expand Triple Elm, and I might expand it all the way, or I might expand it halfway into that space and maybe just have another.

339
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:12,760
As you know, Chrissy and Nick are going to open up the farm stand, and it's possible they might want to rent out some of that.

340
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:16,480
No chance of convincing you to put a bar there.

341
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:17,220
What?

342
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:19,820
No chance of convincing you to put a bar there.

343
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:20,780
Sheddy's is going to be a bar.

344
00:28:21,780 --> 00:28:23,000
It's going to be for Sheddy's Pub.

345
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:24,960
Then you really need more parking.

346
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:30,820
Well, maybe you could lose the landscaping in the front.

347
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:33,800
Brian, do you have more parking spots?

348
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:34,220
I don't know.

349
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:34,760
Is that?

350
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:36,820
That's next to the state highway.

351
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:38,340
It's a nice little building, too.

352
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:41,560
I just had a quick thing for you guys.

353
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:57,040
So I just want to make sure I'm clear here is that the new proposed building, that lower building, would be serviced by what is now that gravel decline from the existing Braschetti's parking lot, right?

354
00:28:57,140 --> 00:28:59,060
That would be the access for that building?

355
00:28:59,480 --> 00:28:59,840
Yes.

356
00:29:00,020 --> 00:29:02,700
And then the other driveway is for the residential home, right?

357
00:29:02,940 --> 00:29:03,380
That's right.

358
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:06,020
Tom, can you go over and show Brian on the map?

359
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:07,760
I'm just trying to make it clear.

360
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:08,140
You good?

361
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:08,780
I got it right here.

362
00:29:09,060 --> 00:29:09,220
All right.

363
00:29:09,260 --> 00:29:11,860
I just want to make sure before I get to my next question.

364
00:29:13,420 --> 00:29:33,920
With the proposed driveway and possible increased traffic, are you guys looking to stop or change or will there be an impact to the citizens that now currently use, I guess, where that new building would go, parking ATV trailers and snowmobile trailers and trail access there?

365
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:40,980
Are you looking to stop people from using that to park trucks and trailers for their off-road vehicles?

366
00:29:40,980 --> 00:29:42,700
Are you talking about outside the parking lot?

367
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:55,860
Yeah, outside the parking lot on the street, so it would be like right on that fence line because it's going to run right up against the entrance and exit to that residential parking, residential driveway, as well as if there's increased traffic coming in and out of this one exit.

368
00:29:55,860 --> 00:30:07,000
I'm just curious if you're planning on doing something about it or if you thought about that when you put the driveway in, if that was a consideration for the state.

369
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:17,540
Because you've got 400 line of sight when no one's there, but when you park a dually there towing a trailer with four quads on it, it might hinder the sight line a little bit.

370
00:30:17,660 --> 00:30:18,100
That's a good point.

371
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:22,060
I mean, we're definitely going to have to do something with a shoulder there anyway.

372
00:30:22,580 --> 00:30:29,740
I know that, so it may be a situation where I make it so it's not going to be a place where people can park.

373
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:35,740
Well, technically, the DOT will tell you that you're not supposed to park in there right-of-way.

374
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:50,320
So those, you know, trailers with four-wheelers on them and stuff that might park there today, technically they're not supposed to park in a DOT right-of-way.

375
00:30:51,740 --> 00:31:00,020
You know, with the towns on Depot Road right-of-way, Fremont Road right-of-way, well, that's a different matter.

376
00:31:00,020 --> 00:31:08,120
But, you know, I've never seen a DOT driveway permit issued that doesn't have a standard condition, no parking in the right-of-way.

377
00:31:08,340 --> 00:31:08,440
Right.

378
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:10,400
And I bet yours says that, too.

379
00:31:12,380 --> 00:31:16,460
Is there any detail on that right-of-way on any of these plans?

380
00:31:17,460 --> 00:31:26,120
The right-of-way is if you go to sheet, well, I guess start with sheet one, which is sheet two, actually.

381
00:31:26,460 --> 00:31:28,820
Liam, which is the existing conditions plan.

382
00:31:30,020 --> 00:31:46,560
The front line of the site, this line here, is coincident, that's Dave's westerly parcel boundary, is coincident with the easterly line of Main Street.

383
00:31:47,220 --> 00:31:57,680
And then you'll see, as you head north, there is a State of New Hampshire parcel that's actually the Rockingham Trail.

384
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:58,220
Right.

385
00:31:58,220 --> 00:32:03,880
And then beyond that is Town Right-of-way for Depot Road.

386
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:17,840
So if you collectively, that series of line segments form the limits of public right-of-way, some of it's state jurisdiction, some of it's municipal jurisdiction, in that vicinity.

387
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:28,600
Yeah, I just didn't know if there'd be, like, a connect-the-dots through there, you know what I mean?

388
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:30,660
It's kind of a funky angle.

389
00:32:32,380 --> 00:32:33,820
It's broken up by the towns.

390
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:39,340
I mean, I think the funky angle is from the fact that there was a railroad thing.

391
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:39,940
Right.

392
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:40,540
Right.

393
00:32:40,540 --> 00:32:52,200
I mean, it's a state issue regardless, so it's really not on us, like you said, but I would just, I guess I would be curious to see what the state's thoughts are on that, because it is a...

394
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:53,680
They're pretty good about it.

395
00:32:53,780 --> 00:32:54,480
They're pretty smart.

396
00:32:54,480 --> 00:33:04,200
I mean, I think what they will do is they will look at the driveway permit applications, and there's two, right?

397
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:13,860
There's the driveway application for the, for the northerly driveway, which would be for the existing home.

398
00:33:15,060 --> 00:33:27,380
It's limited, and then there's the modification of the existing commercial driveway at 323, that, you know, probably there's not going to be anything done to it.

399
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:43,040
It'll just be, the permit will be amended to acknowledge that what's shown on this plan and what was shown on the prior plan, that approved it in the first place, you know, collectively can use it, right?

400
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:46,960
That would be my anticipation.

401
00:33:47,660 --> 00:33:49,560
Is that what you applied for, isn't it, Tom?

402
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:50,920
Yeah, it would be, yeah.

403
00:33:51,940 --> 00:33:54,580
Did you have a plan B if the state has a problem with it?

404
00:33:54,580 --> 00:33:58,500
As far as the driveway entrance for the residents?

405
00:33:59,300 --> 00:33:59,420
Yeah.

406
00:34:00,380 --> 00:34:10,620
From what I understand, reading the state's requirements, is that every parcel is required if it has frontage on a DOT road.

407
00:34:11,420 --> 00:34:17,620
They need to be, they have to issue a driveway permit, assuming you meet the requirements for it.

408
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:27,820
In this case, where this parcel only has frontage on the DOT roadway, I, you know, we meet the sight distance there.

409
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:33,940
I think that's really as far as they can kind of look for a residential driveway.

410
00:34:33,940 --> 00:34:52,240
Like Steve was saying, as far as, you know, other people parking in the right-of-way or that, I think that's kind of almost beyond what Dave can do, just in that he also doesn't necessarily have the authority to do anything in the right-of-way.

411
00:34:52,240 --> 00:35:08,880
Yeah, I mean, that parcel isn't the same configuration that existed on the date of enactment of the New Hampshire driveway statute, which is July 1st, 1971.

412
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:18,900
I know that the lines have adjusted, David adjusted, but for that parcel that he purchased from the church, you are correct.

413
00:35:19,020 --> 00:35:23,940
He has entitlement to a driveway curb cut on that parcel, right?

414
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:40,540
I mean, obviously, when the state enacted the driveway statute, if they would refuse somebody a driveway permit on an existing law of record, they would be taken.

415
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:42,720
Right. It's not legal.

416
00:35:44,160 --> 00:35:46,040
Unless they wanted to write out a check.

417
00:35:48,580 --> 00:35:53,560
So, I think you'll make that work there.

418
00:35:54,900 --> 00:36:01,220
But the plan B, I suppose, would be to connect the house to the commercial driveway, right?

419
00:36:02,440 --> 00:36:02,920
Right.

420
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:10,460
But I suspect that there will probably be no need for a permit, just because of the law.

421
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:16,660
You'd have to find out what the feedback was from the state first before you could adjust to it.

422
00:36:16,660 --> 00:36:20,100
Basically, it would come in the acid test in the form of a permit or not.

423
00:36:21,160 --> 00:36:21,400
Okay.

424
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:23,200
Yeah.

425
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,680
Anybody else have a question for the applicant?

426
00:36:29,340 --> 00:36:30,920
One last one that I would ask.

427
00:36:31,140 --> 00:36:36,180
I know you said the floor permits that Steve mentioned are in progress with the state right now.

428
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:36,420
Yep.

429
00:36:36,420 --> 00:36:39,600
We didn't get a letter from the fire chief yet.

430
00:36:39,900 --> 00:36:41,700
Has he had a dialogue with you guys?

431
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:45,660
I've talked to him a couple different times, so we're working things out.

432
00:36:45,740 --> 00:36:50,740
He's told me what he's looking for and what he needs to figure out what we need for fire protection.

433
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:51,420
Yep.

434
00:36:51,420 --> 00:36:59,960
So, and I made some phone calls today, so I'm getting people on board and getting engineers to look at the building and what we're going to use it for.

435
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:09,280
And that's all Mike right now is looking for, for an engineer to say, here's what you need for the building according to the IFC code.

436
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:11,900
So, we're working on that, yeah.

437
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:12,860
All right.

438
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:15,000
I'm not sure what other issues there'd be.

439
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:19,760
Maybe access, that sort of thing, but he seems to be fine with the plans.

440
00:37:20,020 --> 00:37:23,160
Yeah, they like getting the trucks behind buildings and all that stuff.

441
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:23,420
Yeah.

442
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:24,220
Okay.

443
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:25,620
All right.

444
00:37:25,620 --> 00:37:32,880
Well, we don't have anybody from the public out there right now to send the questions back.

445
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:44,360
So, really, it's just going to come back up here to the board if anybody's comfortable doing a conditional approval.

446
00:37:44,700 --> 00:37:45,540
Conditional approval.

447
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:45,920
Yep.

448
00:37:46,200 --> 00:37:48,400
Because it went blank for a second there.

449
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:53,420
It just speeds up the process, and yet it's going to be all done properly.

450
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:53,960
Yeah.

451
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:56,840
Yeah, I just, I wish we had the fire chief's letter here, too.

452
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,560
Then I wouldn't mind waiting for the state.

453
00:37:59,380 --> 00:38:01,220
I don't foresee any real problem.

454
00:38:01,480 --> 00:38:05,360
Just whether or not the board's comfortable moving forward without the fire chief tonight.

455
00:38:05,500 --> 00:38:08,040
Yeah, I'm comfortable with it because I know he's at conference.

456
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:09,380
Okay.

457
00:38:10,860 --> 00:38:12,480
People will talk to him?

458
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:13,680
Yeah.

459
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:15,520
He talked to him Friday.

460
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:17,660
I talked to him a couple weeks ago.

461
00:38:17,940 --> 00:38:20,100
So, we're going to make sure it's right.

462
00:38:20,580 --> 00:38:23,340
I think most of us would be in concern.

463
00:38:23,340 --> 00:38:29,420
I mean, the chief divine would be something that would be implemented at the building permit stage anyways.

464
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:29,800
Yeah.

465
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:31,900
Stuff going on inside the building, right?

466
00:38:31,980 --> 00:38:33,180
Your fire protection system.

467
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:34,320
Very close system.

468
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:36,920
I mean, life safety is going to be what he's looking for.

469
00:38:37,060 --> 00:38:37,200
Right.

470
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:38,180
Yeah.

471
00:38:38,180 --> 00:38:41,640
Whereas the site portion of it is usually NFPA1.

472
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:43,560
You mentioned that with the circulation.

473
00:38:44,020 --> 00:38:44,840
Can he get the truck?

474
00:38:45,020 --> 00:38:45,580
Yeah, the truck.

475
00:38:45,720 --> 00:38:47,060
Where he needs to have it, right?

476
00:38:47,060 --> 00:38:47,180
Yeah.

477
00:38:47,180 --> 00:38:53,600
But you got to, I mean, even if you needed to make an adjustment, like where that rain garden is and stuff, right?

478
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:58,900
You could probably punch out some of that or if you felt he needed to do that.

479
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:01,740
Mike usually isn't bashful about telling us what he wants.

480
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:02,380
Yeah.

481
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:03,980
Because usually we would already have a letter.

482
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:07,120
But I think, like you said, you're waiting for some engineers to go back and forth.

483
00:39:07,420 --> 00:39:07,580
Yeah.

484
00:39:07,580 --> 00:39:09,020
So that they can finalize it.

485
00:39:09,680 --> 00:39:10,040
Okay.

486
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:10,920
Yeah.

487
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:13,860
Plus, we'll have to have the letter before anything's finalized anyway.

488
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:15,380
Yeah, it still has to go through.

489
