In a nutshell, there's a provision in our zoning ordinance for the open space development that requires submission of documents,

975
01:00:42,360 --> 01:00:52,000
condominium documents, or the deal with the preservation or management ownership and management of open spaces and so on and so forth.

976
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:54,080
It's a part of the zoning ordinance.

977
01:00:54,200 --> 01:00:55,300
It's been there from day one.

978
01:00:56,800 --> 01:01:07,000
And we collect, at the time you folks are considering a possible approval of an application, draft copies of those documents,

979
01:01:07,000 --> 01:01:15,760
and your town's attorney reviews them for compliance with regard to things that affect the town of Sandown.

980
01:01:15,840 --> 01:01:21,980
In other words, your zoning compliance, if it's age-restricted, how that's going to be handled, then those types of things.

981
01:01:22,000 --> 01:01:37,980
Apparently, Nancy, the correspondence that she sent us was, they're looking at doing amendments that don't, to their declaration,

982
01:01:37,980 --> 01:01:47,580
that don't affect things that we look at for zoning compliance.

983
01:01:47,900 --> 01:01:49,360
The open space piece of it.

984
01:01:49,400 --> 01:01:49,600
Yeah.

985
01:01:49,740 --> 01:01:51,520
It's, you know, it's not that aspect.

